## Prerequisites

- .NET 10 SDK
- Docker (for local development)
- AWS credentials configured (role: see vertical enrollment)

## Getting Started

```bash
dotnet restore
dotnet build
dotnet test
```

## Running Locally

{{- if model.manifest.database != null }}

Create the database tables first{{ if model.manifest.tenant_ready }} (including the `tenants` table; without it, tenant-protected endpoints return 503){{ end }}:

```bash
dotnet ef database update --project src/{{ model.names.namespace }}
```

Then run the service:
{{- end }}

```bash
dotnet run --project src/{{ model.names.namespace }}
```

## Configuration

Configuration is loaded from `appsettings.json` and environment-specific overrides.
Secrets are stored in AWS Secrets Manager at `{env}/{{ model.manifest.product }}/{{ model.manifest.service_name }}/config`.
